  "rules": "Every compatibility marker the product recognises: `*Protocol` keys (a string literal matching the pattern, or a serde field whose snake_case name ends in `_protocol`), `FIELD`/`*_FIELD` extension constants, `deny_unknown_fields` struct fields and run-ledger allowlist fields, with one writer, one reader, the change that introduced it and the condition under which it may be retired; plus the stored-line kinds, environment controls and exact text values listed below. check_compatibility_markers.py reads src/ against this table: every recognised marker or record field must have a row of its kind, a row must be present in src/, and every row must carry a retirement condition. A key that is both a protocol key and a record field has one row per kind. Rows of kind record-kind, env and text are presence-checked only: the check fails when the value is absent from a named file, but a new stored line kind, environment control or message is not discovered. A record-field row names a field the release introduced after the previous release's snapshot (tests/fixtures/release-record-fields.txt); rows stay listed once the snapshot holds them, so the table is a superset of the source-derived additions, and they are the record fields tests/release_integrity/record_fields.rs requires in the CHANGELOG's mixed-version paragraph.",
